<!--
  Square-canvas variant of ic_lenta_logo.xml for the Splash Screen API's icon slot. Android
  12+'s SplashScreen system forces the icon drawable into a fixed square working area and
  applies a circular/adaptive-icon-style mask to it — a wide wordmark placed at full width gets
  stretched to fill that square and then cropped illegibly by the circle. Padding the viewport
  out to a square (420x420, vs. the wordmark's native 164x42) and centering the artwork inside
  it keeps the whole wordmark within the mask's safe zone, so it renders small but intact
  instead of getting clipped to an unreadable fragment.

  The path is ic_lenta_logo.xml's, and the translate below is what centres it: keep the two in
  step, including the translateX, which changed with the wordmark's width when ".RU" came off.
-->
